From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/grate: gr3d: accept relocations on the PSEQ command odd slots

The Tegra30 3D pixel sequencer takes its commands as (even, odd) register
pairs, PSEQ_COMMAND_EVEN(n) at 0x520 + 2n and PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(n) at
0x521 + 2n. A DMA command, which NVIDIA's driver uses to load the program
and the constants of a fragment program with more than one epoch, carries
the word count in the even slot and a buffer address in the odd slot.

The Grate command stream patcher (uapi/patching.c) replaces the payload of
every write to a register in gr3d_addr_regs[] with the DMA address of the
buffer named by the relocation descriptor. The PSEQ odd slots were not in
the list, so the descriptor that userspace places there reached the
sequencer unpatched and the DMA never read the buffer.

Add the 16 odd slots to the list. As for every address register, every
word written to an odd slot is now a relocation descriptor: a write of a
literal zero is read as bo_index 0, bo_offset 0, and fails the job if it
has no buffer. A userspace that clears the command slots must therefore
write the even slots only. A command that does not use its odd slot
(execute, tail) must do the same.

This replaces the earlier version of this patch, which edited
drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gr3d.c. That file is only built with
CONFIG_DRM_TEGRA_ORIG, not by the kernel this tree ships.

Not tested on hardware when written.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/gr3d.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/gr3d.h
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #define GR3D_QR_CZ_ADDR			0x419
 #define GR3D_TEX_TEX_ADDR(x)		(0x710 + (x))
 #define GR3D_DW_MEMORY_OUTPUT_ADDRESS	0x904
+#define GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(x)	(0x521 + (x) * 2)
 #define GR3D_GLOBAL_SURFADDR(x)		(0xe00 + (x))
 #define GR3D_GLOBAL_SPILLSURFADDR	0xe2a
 #define GR3D_GLOBAL_SURFOVERADDR(x)	(0xe30 + (x))
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/gr3d.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/grate/gr3d.c
@@ -247,6 +247,22 @@
 	GR3D_TEX_TEX_ADDR(14),
 	GR3D_TEX_TEX_ADDR(15),
 	GR3D_DW_MEMORY_OUTPUT_ADDRESS,
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 0),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 1),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 2),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 3),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 4),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 5),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 6),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 7),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 8),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD( 9),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(10),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(11),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(12),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(13),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(14),
+	GR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_ODD(15),
 	GR3D_GLOBAL_SURFADDR( 0),
 	GR3D_GLOBAL_SURFADDR( 1),
 	GR3D_GLOBAL_SURFADDR( 2),
